    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15005" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dȳme</span></b> , ēs, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δύμη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an old sea-coast town in Achaia</i>, <i>west of Olenos</i>, now perhaps <i>Kaminitza</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 5, 6, §
			13</span></i>.—Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dȳmae</span></b> , ārum,
			f., <i><span class="en">Liv. 27, 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38,
			29</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dȳmaeus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Dymae</i>, <i>Dymaean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 31 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dȳmaei</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the Dymaeans</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 16, 1</span></i>.</div>
